      "alt": "Conceptual diagram of affine recalibration. Left panel: raw predictions form a narrow distribution centred to the right of a wider target population. Right panel: after the map y-prime = mu_t + rho times sigma_t times (y-hat minus mu_p) over sigma_p, the predictions are centred on the target mean with spread rho times sigma_t, still narrower than the target. Below, a rank strip connects each raw prediction to its recalibrated value; no lines cross, so Spearman and Kendall are unchanged while R-squared and the error metrics are not."
